      "text": "### Book Summary\n**Title**: Stochastic Governance: Probabilistic Approaches to Policy Design Under Uncertainty  \n**Authors**: Vasilis Papadimitriou and Sakura Nishihara  \n**Year**: 2021  \n**Publisher**: MIT Policy Press  \n**ISBN**: 978-0-26203-847-1  \n\nThis 312-page technical monograph applies Bayesian inference and stochastic optimization to the design of public policies under deep uncertainty. The authors argue that conventional policy analysis frameworks, which rely on deterministic projections and point estimates, often underperform in contexts characterized by non-stationary risks and contested model assumptions. They introduce the concept of the \"adaptive policy envelope,\" which treats policy commitments as probability distributions over outcome spaces rather than fixed prescriptions. This approach allows for policy revisions based on new evidence without causing credibility crises.\n\nKey Themes:\n- Bayesian policy analysis\n- Deep uncertainty\n- Adaptive governance\n- Stochastic optimization\n- Policy design\n- Decision theory\n- Uncertainty quantification\n\nThe book also includes three extended case studies:\n1. Climate adaptation policy in the Netherlands\n2. Pandemic response protocol design\n3. Infrastructure investment under seismic risk\n\n### Authors' Background\n**Vasilis Papadimitriou** is a Professor of Public Policy at the Harvard Kennedy School. His research focuses on Bayesian policy analysis, adaptive governance, and deep uncertainty. He earned his PhD in Operations Research from MIT in 2003. His notable publications include:\n- \"Stochastic Governance\" (MIT Policy Press, 2021)\n- \"Adaptive Policy Envelopes under Deep Uncertainty\" (Policy Sciences, 2018)\n- \"Bayesian Updating in Multi-Stakeholder Policy Contexts\" (Journal of Policy Analysis and Management, 2015)\n\nHe is also a co-editor of \"Uncertainty and Governance: A Reader\" (MIT Press, 2019).\n\nFor further details on Vasilis Papadimitriou, you can explore more through his profile [here](https://example.com/authors/vasilis-papadimitriou). \n\nThis information should provide a solid foundation for your graduate seminar on the applications of Bayesian methods in policy design.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
