    {
      "text": "### Book Information\n**Title:** Stochastic Governance: Probabilistic Approaches to Policy Design Under Uncertainty  \n**Authors:** Vasilis Papadimitriou and Sakura Nishihara  \n**Year:** 2021  \n**Publisher:** MIT Policy Press  \n**ISBN:** 978-0-26203-847-1  \n\n**Summary:**  \nThis 312-page technical monograph applies Bayesian inference and stochastic optimization to the design of public policies under deep uncertainty. The authors argue that traditional policy analysis methods, which rely on deterministic projections and point estimates, often fall short in situations characterized by fluctuating risks and conflicting model assumptions. They introduce the concept of the \"adaptive policy envelope,\" where policy commitments are viewed as probability distributions over potential outcomes rather than fixed directives. This allows for policy adjustments based on new evidence without jeopardizing credibility. The monograph includes detailed case studies on climate adaptation in the Netherlands, designing pandemic response protocols, and managing infrastructure investment amidst seismic risks.\n\n**Key Themes:**\n- Bayesian policy analysis\n- Deep uncertainty\n- Adaptive governance\n- Stochastic optimization\n- Policy design\n- Decision theory\n- Uncertainty quantification\n\n### Author Background\n\n**Vasilis Papadimitriou**\n- **Position:** Professor of Public Policy at Harvard Kennedy School\n- **Research Interests:** Focuses on Bayesian policy analysis, adaptive governance, and deep uncertainty.\n- **Education:** PhD in Operations Research from MIT (2003).\n- **Notable Publications:**\n  - *Stochastic Governance* (MIT Policy Press, 2021)\n  - \"Adaptive Policy Envelopes under Deep Uncertainty\" (Policy Sciences, 2018)\n  - \"Bayesian Updating in Multi-Stakeholder Policy Contexts\" (Journal of Policy Analysis and Management, 2015)\n- **Editorial Work:** Co-editor of *Uncertainty and Governance: A Reader* (MIT Press, 2019).\n\nFor more information, you can view his [faculty profile here](https://openbooks.net/authors/vasilis-papadimitriou).\n\n**Sakura Nishihara** — While I didn't retrieve specific information about Sakura Nishihara in this search, you can look up additional sources or academic profiles for her contributions and background.\n\nThis monograph and the authors' expertise can provide valuable insights for your seminar, especially regarding probabilistic policy design and adaptive governance strategies.",
